  "steps": [
    "Heat the oven to 180°C and line a 20cm round tin. Whisk all the dry ingredients together in a large bowl.",
    "Make a well and add the oat milk, olive oil, vinegar and vanilla. Whisk just until smooth — don't overmix.",
    "Pour the batter into the tin and bake for 32–35 minutes, until a skewer comes out with only a few moist crumbs.",
    "Cool completely in the tin before turning out.",
    "Pour over the melted dark chocolate and let it set into a glossy top before slicing."
  ],
  "notes": "Use a fruity, mild olive oil rather than a peppery one. The cake keeps moist for days in a tin — if it lasts that long."
}
